@copilot Follow up on the CI compatibility fix in commit 59a8a833f2ce28b3eeb3322ce96960afcbe99743, directly on this PR. Keep semconv 1.45.0, maintenance/v2.x, the current ready-for-review state, the JMX JVM registry fix, previous CI compatibility changes, and all emitted telemetry unchanged. Commit and push only this scoped correction to the same PR head; do not create another PR. Leave review replies and thread resolution to the coordinator.

The latest-head Copilot review https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/21147#pullrequestreview-5758227948 found five valid violations of .github/instructions/java-style.instructions.md's Suppressions rule: @SuppressWarnings belongs on the one member that needs it, and on a class only when multiple members need the same warning. The prior CI fix added class-level deprecation suppression although the deprecated semconv constants occur in one method per affected class. Move each annotation and its concise explanation from class to method: KafkaConnectBatchRecordAttributes.getLinkAttributes() (review comment 4459419184); RocketMqProducerAttributeExtractor.onStart() (4459419242); RocketMqReceiveBatchMessageAttributeExtractor.onStart() (4459419279); RocketMqReceiveSpanLinksExtractor.extract() (4459419332); SpringRabbitExtraAttributesExtractor.onStart() (4459419382). Inspect other class-level deprecation suppressions newly added by the same CI fix for this exact style issue; keep class scope where multiple members require it. Do not remove needed suppression or mask additional deprecated usage.

Run the narrow relevant spotlessApply, compilation with OtelDeprecatedApiUsage enabled, and affected Kafka Connect, RocketMQ and Spring Rabbit tests/compatibility variants. Acceptance criteria: these five suppressions are member-scoped, any other single-member class suppression introduced by the prior fix is narrowed, previously fixed compilation and JMX behavior remain correct, and legacy messaging telemetry remains unchanged.

