Review https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/21147#pullrequestreview-5758617412 contains a body-only, unpublished finding that needed human assessment. I verified the actual code and the .github/instructions/java-style.instructions.md Suppressions rule: instrumentation/rabbitmq-2.7/javaagent/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent/instrumentation/rabbitmq/v2_7/ReactorRabbitMqTest.java has @SuppressWarnings("deprecation") on the class, but only testShouldNotFailDeclaringExchange() uses the intentionally retained deprecated MESSAGING_SYSTEM constant. Move that suppression and its succinct explanation to this test method, leaving the class's other annotations, the intentionally disabled latest-deps condition, and the assertion unchanged. I checked other class-level suppressions introduced in this PR; those have deprecated uses in multiple members and should stay as they are.

Run the narrow RabbitMQ test formatting and compilation with OtelDeprecatedApiUsage enabled, plus the relevant test if feasible. Preserve the existing key and compatibility variants. No new issue or comment thread is required for this body-only review finding.
